# Read the gold a Craft repair asks for, against the item's own hit points and
# base value (bd inc-nc1). tools/check_repair_cost.sh reads the three dumps.
#
# WHY THIS FIXTURE. The fixture is the built human-paladin-seed4-opt0822. He
# wears leather armour +3, a 2136 gp item that is not metal, so Craft needs no
# forge. He carries 11 gp, so the repair stops at "That would cost N gp in
# materials, but you only have 11 gp." -- the same gpCost the Proceed prompt
# prints, with nothing spent.
#
# THE ARMOUR IS DAMAGED HERE by the wizard entry "Damage Worn Armour" (bd
# inc-10v7f), 5 points: 81 of 86 hit points. No trap, no roll.
#
# WHAT IS DUMPED. exam: the item's description ("base value of N gp", "N out of
# M hit points"). menu: the "Repair which item?" list with (hp/max). cost: the
# gold message.

@until "Things in View" ESC
s*3     # search: real turns, so the harness counts this as a played session

w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Damage Worn Armour"
"5" ENTER
@until "Things in View" ESC

i
j
x
@dump:exam
ESC
ESC

u
@choose "Craft"
r
@dump:menu
a
@dump:cost
